<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n94630" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκάφιον</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ᾰ]</span> (A) (not <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκαφίον</span>), τό, 
			Dim. of
		
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκάφη</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>small bowl</i> or <i>basin</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>CP</u>
				4.16.3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PLond.</u>
				2.402
			</span></i><i><span class="en">
				 ii 13
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii B.C.)</span>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PHamb.</u>
				10.36
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii A.D.)</span>, etc.; used in baths, <i><span class="en">
				Lyc.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				11.501f
			</span></i>; <i>small cup</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Phylarch.
				44
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">J., <u>Inscr.Délos</u>
				442</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>B</u>
				43
			</span></i>, al. <span class="entity">(ii B.C.)</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>woman's chamberpot</i> or <i>nightstool</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Th.</u>
				633
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Eup.
				46
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>a fashion of haircutting</i> (borrowed from the Scythians),
				<i>in which the hair was cut close off round the head</i>, so
			as to leave it only on the crown, which then looked
			like a <i>bowl</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκάφιον ἀποκεκαρμένη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Th.</u>
					838
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ς. ἀποτετιλμένος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Av.</u>
					806
				</span></i>
			: hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>crown</i> of the head, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἵνα μὴ
				καταγῇς τὸ ς</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				604
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b>
			<i>occiput</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ruf.
				<u>Oss.</u>
				2
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>c.</b> name of a
			bandage for the head, <i><span class="en">
				Sor.
				<u>Fasc.</u>
				3
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b> in pl.,
				=
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰσχία, τά</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				2.183
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>IV.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκαφεῖον</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Fract.</u>
				8
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
